    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0613" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/299.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-07-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Congress, which opens August 10, will probably award Guayaquil contract. It
                    might be well for the Department to find out if MacArthur Bros. are in earnest.
                    If so a representative should be sent immediately or the local representative be
                    given full powers to negotiate and sign contract. This firm is the only entirely
                    American house interested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
